namespace lore {
inline const std::vector<std::string> INTRO = {"Long ago, a forgotten dwarven clan unearthed the Pyreheart: the molten crystal core that kept the world warm. In their devotion, they dug too deep beneath its altar and woke the Ashen King. The fallen god slaughtered the clan, ripped the crystal from the stone, and forced it into his own hollowed chest.", "", "With the earth's heart stolen, a slow frost gripped the world. Across the dying lands, scattered settlements struggle to survive the bitter cold, none more cursed than Charnfen. Built unknowingly atop the collapsed dwarven mines, this bleak backwater town clung for generations to the strange, sickly heat leaking from the ground, blind to the truth that they were warming themselves on the fever of the sleeping god below.", "", "Now, the Ashen King stirs beneath the town. Ash poisons the wells, the soil reeks of fever, and the dead claw their way out of the graveyard mud, drawn downward by the cursed heartbeat below. You have traveled to Charnfen at the edge of ruin. Descend into the filth, and tear the heart back out."};
inline const std::vector<std::vector<std::string>> ACT_OPEN = {{"THE CRYPT", "Beneath Charnfen's cracked gravestones, the wet dirt is warm like fresh meat. Bloated corpses and ash-caked skeletons stalk the flooded tombs, their shattered ribs glowing with a sickly, dark ember."}, {"THE CAVES", "Beyond the breached crypt walls lie the old dwarven mines. Sightless, hairless beasts and giant rats have mutated in the unnatural heat, their blistered skin hardened into armour dripping with black grease."}, {"THE FORGE", "The smoke-filled halls of the fallen dwarves echo again with iron on iron. Iron golems and half-melted smiths hurl bone and scrap into the relit fires, forging cursed weapons for their master."}, {"THE DEEP", "The scorched pit of the Cinderfire, among rivers of boiling metal and charred bone. Somewhere below, the stolen Pyreheart beats behind blackened ribs."}, {"THE CISTERN", "Vast, echoing caverns of stone basins and wide aqueducts, where the dwarves once gathered pure, cold water. Now the channels are choked with grey ash, and the basins hold only black sludge with a greasy, acidic sheen."}, {"THE CITY", "The silent, ash-buried capital of the dwarven kingdom fills a colossal cavern. Cracked streets wind between carved stone houses, empty market stalls and fallen statues, and white bones lie across the squares."}, {"THE VAULTS", "Behind half-melted iron doors lie the treasuries and archives of the dead: shattered chests, collapsed shelves, ash-covered scrolls, and heaps of tarnished coin fused to the stone in the pitch dark."}, {"THE BARRACKS", "Long, low halls of rough stone where the dwarven army lived and drilled. Rotten bunks, overturned weapon racks and scorched banners, and in the yards the dead still march in step."}, {"THE PRISON", "A shattered dungeon carved into the black rock. Broken chains lie coiled across the flagstones like dead iron snakes, leading to a torn-open vault door at the centre."}, {"THE SANCTUM", "A scorched temple of polished black stone around a raised platform. On it stands the empty altar where the Pyreheart once burned, and behind it the floor gives way to a hole dug recklessly deep."}};
inline const std::vector<std::vector<std::string>> WRITINGS = {
    {"A gravestone: 'Here lies Wenna, who kept the well. Taken by the cough, like her mother.'", "Scratched on a coffin lid from the inside: 'not dead not dead not dead'", "A sexton's note: 'Third grave open this week. The ash gets into everything, even the shrouds.'", "A prayer card: 'Warm ground, keep our roots alive and our dead asleep.'", "A child's slate: 'Mam says the floor is warm because the old ones under it are still working.'"},
    {"Dwarven runes on a pit prop, and under them in chalk: 'NO ONE LEFT TO READ THESE'", "A Charnfen digger's tally: forty marks, then the word 'HOT' pressed deep into the wood.", "A torn page: '...the rats grow big as dogs down here. Their skin is like boot leather, and it sweats black...'", "A dwarven skull, small and broad, with a pickaxe still in its hands.", "A lamp, cold, and a note: 'Listen to the walls. Something down there has a heartbeat.'"},
    {"Carved over a forge in the old tongue, and scratched beside it in common: 'The Heart provides.'", "A dwarven ledger, the last page: 'We dig beneath the altar. The crystal sings louder every day.'", "Burnt into a door: 'The smiths did not stop when they died. They only stopped screaming.'", "A child's iron toy, dwarf-made, half melted into the floor.", "A golem's work order, still in its chest: 'Feed the fire. Feed the fire. Feed the fire.'"},
    {"Words in the heat-shimmer, in no voice at all: 'I was a god when your mountains were sand.'", "A broken chain, each link as thick as a man. The seal on it is dwarven, and very old.", "Ash shaped into letters: 'THE HEART IS MINE. COME AND TAKE IT.'", "A dwarven altar, cracked in two. Something large was torn out of it.", "A last prayer, half burnt: 'Sun-Breath, Deep-Tide, Cinderfire: forgive us. We only wanted to be warm.'"},
    {"Chiseled into a mossy keystone: 'Before the theft, the Deep-Tide sang through these aqueducts, pure and cold as glacier melt.'", "In white chalk across a rusted floodgate: 'Do not kneel to drink from the pools. The water remembers every corpse that drowned within it.'", "A sluice-keeper's log, the last entry: 'We dropped the heavy grates to keep the swell from the lower halls. The water rose anyway, thick as tar and warm to the touch.'", "Chalked on the wall of a pump house, in big letters: 'DO NOT DRINK'", "A dwarven water-gauge, its needle rusted fast at a mark labelled in the old tongue: 'never'."},
    {"A shop sign, the paint blistered off: a hammer, a loaf, and a name nobody can read any more.", "Chalked on a door: 'Counted forty in this street. Forty, and not one of them fell over.'", "A census tablet of the dwarves: 'Ten thousand hearths.' Someone has scratched out the last nought, and then the next.", "A child's ball of carved stone, rolled into a gutter of ash.", "On the plinth of a fallen statue: 'The Mayor keeps the city. The city keeps the Heart.'"},
    {"A vault ledger: 'Deposited, one crystal shard, warm. Withdrawn: the hand that held it.'", "Scratched beside a lock: 'Do not count the coins. The coins count you.'", "An archivist's slip: 'Scrolls on the Heart moved to the inner vault. Key to the guardian, as always.'", "A melted crown, fused to the floor in a puddle of gold. It was small: a child's.", "Ash in the shape of a word on a shelf, where a book has burned away: 'MINE'."},
    {"A duty roster, every name struck through, and at the bottom in another hand: 'still on watch'.", "Carved into a bunk: 'Third winter under the mountain. The fires never go out, and we are always cold.'", "A drill-yard board: 'Shield, pike, bow. Shield, pike, bow. Hold the line until the line holds you.'", "A scorched banner of the clan, its anvil sign still gold under the soot.", "An order, sealed in red wax: 'No soldier is to go below the Sanctum. Whatever he hears.'"},
    {"Scratched into a cell wall, in rows of five: more days than a man can live.", "A turnkey's tally: 'Cells: two hundred. Prisoners: two hundred. Prisoners after the waking: none. Cells: open.'", "Gouged deep into the stone, from the inside: 'HE IS AWAKE'", "A manacle the size of a cart wheel, torn open. The iron is melted at the break.", "A prisoner's note: 'They say the god below calls us his. They say he will come up through the floor.'"},
    {"A prayer, carved in the black stone: 'Sun-Breath above, Deep-Tide between, Cinderfire beneath. Keep us warm.'", "Melted gold has run down the altar steps and set like wax. Offerings, all of them, to an empty stone.", "A priest's last sermon, half burnt: 'He is not a thief. He is a god taking back what is his.'", "Soot on a pillar, in the shape of a hand reaching down toward the hole.", "A rite-book, open at a page torn out. Only the heading is left: 'How to Bind a God'."}};
inline const std::map<std::string, std::string> BOSS_WAKE = {{"gravewarden", "The Gravewarden rises from the sexton's chair. 'Charnfen's dead are mine to keep.'"}, {"webmother", "Something huge unfolds from the ceiling, blistered and greasy. The Webmother has grown fat on the heat."}, {"furnace", "The great furnace opens like an eye. The Furnace Lord steps out, dripping slag."}, {"sluicekeeper", "A floodgate wheel groans and turns by itself. The Sluice-Keeper drags himself up out of the black, chained to it still."}, {"ashmayor", "Ash shifts on a bronze throne-chair. The Ash-Mayor lifts his iron staff: 'Who walks in my city without leave?'"}, {"hoardwarden", "The mound of gold heaves and rises. Six arms come out of it, and one of them holds the vault key."}, {"ironcaptain", "Iron grinds on iron. The Iron-Captain steps out of the ranks, roaring through his melted visor."}, {"headgaoler", "Chains drag across the stone. The Head-Gaoler comes, a broken manacle swinging from his wrist."}, {"prelate", "Above the empty altar a withered body rises into the air. The High Prelate opens his ribs: there is only cold inside."}, {"ashenking", "On a throne of black stone the Ashen King stands up. Behind his ribs the Pyreheart beats, faster."}};
inline const std::map<std::string, std::string> BOSS_DIES = {{"gravewarden", "The Gravewarden falls apart into old bones and older dust. The way down opens."}, {"webmother", "The Webmother curls up and is still. The webs go slack across the cave."}, {"furnace", "The Furnace Lord cools to black iron and cracks. The anvils of the dwarves fall silent again."}, {"sluicekeeper", "The Sluice-Keeper sinks back into the sludge, and the great wheel finally stops."}, {"ashmayor", "The Ash-Mayor slumps in his chair and does not rise. Grey ash settles over the silent city."}, {"hoardwarden", "The Hoard-Warden sinks into his gold. The heap cools, and is only gold again."}, {"ironcaptain", "The Iron-Captain falls to his knees, and the ranks behind him fall with him."}, {"headgaoler", "The Head-Gaoler crashes down in his own chains. Somewhere a cell door swings open."}, {"prelate", "The High Prelate drops onto the altar and breaks like glass. Cold air sighs up out of the hole behind it."}, {"ashenking", "The Ashen King breaks like a coal under a hammer. You tear the Pyreheart from his chest, and it beats in your hands."}};
inline const std::string WAYSTATION = "A dwarven waystation, empty for an age. A fountain still runs clear here, and someone from Charnfen has set up shop.";
inline const std::vector<std::string> VICTORY = {"With a final, bone-shattering blow, the Ashen King collapses onto the jagged steps of his obsidian throne. Reaching into the scorching ruin of his hollowed chest, you wrap your blistered hands around the Pyreheart and tear the molten crystal free. Deprived of his stolen prize, the fallen god does not die, but shrivels back into a cold, powerless husk of char and brittle bone, doomed to starve in the lightless rock where the dwarves first woke him.", "In your grip, the heavy crystal sheds its crust of black grease and rot. Its violent, choking glare softens into a deep, steady pulse as you press the earth's heart back into the fractured bedrock below. Clean, golden warmth bleeds back into the stone veins of the world, the boiling rivers of slag cool into silent iron, and the god's long fever finally breaks.", "Far above, through miles of collapsed mines, dead halls, and drowned tombs, the mountain draws its first clean breath in ages. In the muddy graveyard of Charnfen, the restless dead collapse back into their broken coffins, the poisoned wells begin to clear, and the bitter frost retreats before a pale, honest dawn. The Pyreheart beats in the earth once more, and the world will not freeze tonight."};
struct Epigraph { std::string text, source; };
inline const std::map<std::string, std::vector<Epigraph>> EPIGRAPHS = {
    {"charnfen", {{"We dug the trenches deeper to keep the dead from clawing back into the streets, yet the mud only grew warmer beneath our spades. By the third week of the grey frost, the soil in the churchyard had turned soft and feverish, sweating a sweet, metallic steam that clung to our wool coats. Last night, the great iron bell in the cracked tower began to toll on its own, slow, heavy strokes that shook the soot from the rafters. Through the shattered stained glass of St. Vane's Cathedral, I watched the grey ash on the headstones drift like living smoke toward the open doors, as if the wind itself were being inhaled by whatever waits at the bottom of the stairs.", "From the Burial Ledger of Sexton Murl, Charnfen's Last Gravedigger"}, {"No prayers are spoken within these walls anymore. The oak pews have rotted into black mulch, the silver candlesticks have slumped into grey puddles upon the stone, and the air tastes of copper, wet wool, and burnt hair. Look closely at the earth between the sunken graves: the coffins have not been dug up from above, they have been split open from within. Every hollow eye in Charnfen turns downward now, drawn by a slow, heavy rhythm pulsing beneath the floorboards of the nave.", "Scratched into the bolted doors of St. Vane's Cathedral"}, {"Three winters ago, we still believed the warmth beneath our boots was a mercy sent to keep our poor village from freezing in the mountain pass. We built our hearths over the old mine-shafts and thanked the silent rock for sparing our children from the frost. Now, the wells run thick with black silt, the elders cough grey dust until their ribs crack, and the dead refuse to lie still in the mud. God have mercy on whoever steps past the broken altar.", "Final entry in the Watchman's Roll, pinned to the lychgate"}, {"Step softly over the sunken graves, traveler. The dead of Charnfen have forgotten their names, their prayers, and their kin, yet every hollow eye turns downward toward the stairs.", "Warning nailed to the lychgate post"}, {"The grey snow never melts on the cathedral roof, though no chill lives in the wind. Every coffin in the yard has split open from the inside out, and the air tastes of copper, wet wool, and burnt hair.", "Journal of a Missing Watchman"}}},
    {"crypt", {{"Beneath the roots of Charnfen's yew trees, the dead do not rot as honest flesh should, they smolder. Through the hairline cracks in the damp limestone, a sick, orange glow pulses in time with a heartbeat far below, slowly cooking the remaining meat off their ribs. We sealed the iron gates with blessed lead and mortared the archways shut with river stone, yet the scratching against the metal never stopped. By dawn, the lead had wept onto the flagstones like silver sweat, and the drowned tombs stood empty.", "Last confession of Mason Garrick, found beside a shattered lantern"}, {"Listen closely when your torch sputters in the dark between the burial niches: that steady, wet sound dripping from the vaulted ceiling is not mountain water. It is the slow, heavy throb of the earth's poisoned veins, thick with soot and old grease. A dead man needs no lantern in these flooded corridors when a stolen coal burns behind his breastbone, lighting the grey mold upon the walls with every shuffling step.", "Carved with a knife into a damp sarcophagus lid"}, {"We carried our fathers down these spiral steps in cedar boxes, believing the cold stone would grant them rest until the end of days. Instead, the rock grew warm as fresh offal, and the dust in their lungs caught fire. Should you hear the rattle of dry bone behind an iron grate, do not call out a name, nothing wearing their faces remembers who they were.", "Fragment from the Charnfen Book of Rites, water-stained and torn"}, {"A dead man needs no torch in these drowned corridors when a stolen coal burns behind his breastbone, lighting the grey mold on the walls.", "Charnfen Grave-Robber's Rhyme"}, {"We sealed the iron gates with blessed lead, yet the scratching never stopped.", "Last words of Sexton Vane"}}},
    {"caves", {{"Where the ancient dwarven picks stopped biting into the mountain, the rock itself began to fester. The heavy oak timbers that once held up the ceiling have turned to brittle charcoal, and the granite sags above our heads like wet clay. Every crack in the uneven floor breathes dry, blistering heat that cracks the lips and turns sweat to salt before it can reach the chin. Stay close to the rusted iron braces, keep a wet rag tied tight over your mouth, and pray the roof holds until you reach the worked stone.", "Surveyor's Slate, Third Dwarven Excavation"}, {"Nothing down here has eyes anymore. Generations ago, when the great furnace woke in the abyss, the beasts trapped in these collapsing tunnels shed their fur and grew plates of cracked, blistered horn. They move in total, suffocating blindness, guided only by the sound of trembling boots on loose gravel and the scent of hot blood. Look at the black grease pooling between the rocks: it is not lamp oil, but the rendered tallow of creatures that crawled too close to the heat and kept on living.", "Rune-stone standing at the border of the Deep-Mines"}, {"Our lanterns died three hundred paces back, choked by the thick, oily air rising from the fissures. Now we navigate by the dull red glow of the cracks beneath our boots and the distant, rhythmic screech of metal echoing up from the dark. Whatever the ancients woke beneath their empire, it has turned the very bones of the mountain into a fevered, sweating beast.", "Scrap of cured leather found inside a collapsed shaft"}, {"Where the dwarves stopped digging, the mountain began to fester.", "Excavation Warden's Note"}, {"Follow the rusted braces, and pray the ceiling holds until you reach the stone halls.", "Dwarven Miner's Scratch"}}},
    {"cistern", {{"Before the theft, the Deep-Tide sang through these carved stone aqueducts, pure and cold as glacier melt, quenching the thirst of ten thousand hearths across the realm. Our water-wheels turned with a gentle, steady grace, carrying life from the mountain's heart to every street and garden. Now, the great stone basins hold only black vinegar choked with floating grey ash, and the air hangs heavy with a sour, blinding stench that blisters the throat.", "Chiseled into the mossy keystone of the Great Sluice"}, {"When the Cinderfire died in the veins of the earth, the underground rivers soured overnight. Trapped in these upper reservoirs above the dead city, the pale, blind things that once swam harmlessly in the dark grew bloated and vicious, feeding on the dead workers and the black ash rising from the shafts below. Do not kneel to drink from the stagnant pools, traveler, though your tongue is cracked and bleeding from the soot, the greasy water remembers every corpse that drowned within it.", "Painted in white chalk across a rusted iron floodgate"}, {"Even the heavy iron gears of the sluice-houses have grown soft with wet rust, groaning like dying cattle as black sludge drips from their teeth. We barred the walkways and dropped the heavy grates to keep the swell from flooding the lower halls, yet the foul water rose anyway, thick as tar and warm to the touch.", "Final entry of the Aqueduct Guild's Logbook"}, {"Do not drink from the basins, though your throat burns with ash. The sludge remembers the dead.", "Warning on the Sluice Wall"}, {"Even the rust down here is wet and bloated.", "Aqueduct Guard's Graffito"}}},
    {"forge", {{"Strike the iron while it screams in the tongs, and feed the bone-coal to the roaring belly of the central furnace. Our leather aprons have melted into our ribs, our eyes have boiled away in the glare, yet the hammer must not fall silent. Driven by a fallen god's fever, the great bellows still heave in the dark, pouring rivers of glowing slag into molds shaped for a war that ended ages ago.", "Hammer-Rune etched into the anvil of Master-Smith Thrain"}, {"Flesh blisters, bone splits, and hair turns to smoke, yet dwarven steel remembers its purpose long after the hand that forged it has turned to cinder. Beware the blinding orange light of the open hearths; it offers no comfort to cold bones, only a relentless, screaming hunger to melt everything down to scrap and weld it into the King's endless army.", "Oath of the Iron-Guild, stamped onto a blackened smelter's mask"}, {"Above the cracked anvils, cold iron chains hang from the smoke-stained pillars like gallows ropes, swaying in the updraft of the furnaces. No living dwarves remain to tend the fires, only mindless iron constructs and scorched, half-melted husks that shovel white bones into the flames without ever pausing to draw breath.", "Chronicle of the Hollow Crown, Chapter IV"}, {"The bellows never rest, for the King demands steel even in his sleep.", "Furnace Inscription"}, {"Beware the glow of the furnaces; it gives no warmth, only the hunger to burn.", "Smelter's Warning"}}},
    {"city", {{"Ten thousand hearths once burned bright beneath this colossal cavern roof, and the ring of silver coins filled the wide stone squares from dawn until dusk. Now, only knee-deep drifts of grey ash remain, and the carved statues of our ancestors weep black soot from their stone eyes. A proud empire built around a stolen sun, reduced in a single night of choking smoke to brittle white bones and silent houses.", "Lament of the Last Scribe, found on a fallen market pillar"}, {"They died with gold in their pockets and grey dust packed tight in their throats, frozen mid-step along the grand stairways as the Cinderfire turned to poison in the vents. Do not disturb the white, calcified heaps piled beside the dry fountains; they were citizens once, huddled together in the dark, waiting for a dawn that never came beneath the mountain.", "Engraved on a tarnished brass street-sign in the High Quarter"}, {"The doors of the great stone houses stand half-buried in drifts of soot, yet behind the shuttered windows, shadows still shuffle across the floorboards. Driven by the hollow echo of their former lives, the burned husks of the city's dead still sweep the grey dust from their steps, blind to the ruin of their kingdom.", "Notes of an unnamed delver, written on dried parchment"}, {"A kingdom built around a stolen sun, buried in a single night of smoke.", "High Square Monument"}, {"Do not disturb the white heaps in the square; they were citizens once.", "Street Warden's Notice"}}},
    {"vaults", {{"Gold does not rust, and cut diamonds do not rot, yet even the purest treasure melts into cursed, shapeless lumps when a god wakes in anger beneath the floorboards. We forged doors three feet thick of blackened steel and barred them with ancient runes of binding, only to trap our own greed inside with the creeping dark.", "Ledger of the Third Archivist, bound in scorched leather"}, {"Heavy locks keep common thieves out, but they cannot hold back the fine grey ash that seeps through keyholes and turns ancient parchment into black, whispering cinders. Look closely at the melted coins fused to the flagstones beneath your boots: each lump of gold still bears the imprint of the charred fingers that tried to carry it out of the smoke.", "Warning pinned to a burned velvet tapestry"}, {"Here lie the treaties, the crowns, and the forgotten histories of a vanished age, rotting in the pitch dark behind half-melted iron bars. Greedy spirits cling to the shattered chests, guarding wealth that can no longer buy bread, water, or a single breath of clean air.", "Inscription above the Inner Treasury Gate"}, {"Heavy doors keep thieves out, and curses in.", "Vault Keeper's Proverb"}, {"Every coin in these halls is welded to the bone of the hand that tried to save it.", "Scratched on a Treasury Pillar"}}},
    {"barracks", {{"No horn ever sounded the retreat, and no captain lived long enough to give the order to stand down. So the blackened ranks still march the cracked training yard in dead silence, gripping melted spears whose shafts have burned straight into their palms. Their shields are warped by heat, their armor welded shut at the joints, yet their dead muscles remain locked in eternal formation.", "Torn Banner of the Iron-Vanguard, recovered from the drill-yard"}, {"We drilled for a hundred years to hold the mountain passes against invaders from the jagged peaks, never dreaming the true monster was sleeping directly beneath our boots. Sharp iron and heavy oak are useless against an enemy made of choking smoke and white-hot cinders.", "Carved into a splintered stone weapon-rack"}, {"The bunks are rotted through, the war-drums have split from the dry heat, and the banners hang like black cobwebs from the rafters. Yet the garrison never abandoned its post, they stand guard over a dead city, waiting to slaughter anyone foolish enough to trespass upon their ruined halls.", "Report of a Dwarven Scout, found clutched in a charred fist"}, {"Shields warped, spears blackened, yet their grip on the haft never loosened.", "Garrison Log"}, {"Sharp iron is useless against an enemy made of smoke and cinders.", "Drill Master's Warning"}}},
    {"prison", {{"Only the pure, crushing weight of the Pyreheart could hold his rot in the dark. Without its living heat pressing down upon the black rock, no chain forged by mortal or god can keep the Ashen King bound. The links were thick as a giant's waist and quenched in dragon-oil, yet they were snapped from the inside out like dry twigs the moment he opened his eyes.", "Ancient Seal Warning, broken in half beside the central pit"}, {"A warden who outlives his prisoner has nothing left to guard in the pitch dark save his own screaming madness and the empty, gouged-out cell. Look at the deep, melted claw-marks dragged across the stone walls, and know the size of the thing that crawled upward toward the temple above.", "Scratched with fingernails into a heavy iron cell door"}, {"The torturers down here grew blind in the smoke long ago, sewing their own eyelids shut with wire so they would not have to look upon the empty chains. Now they patrol the shattered galleries in a frenzy, swinging jagged keys and red-hot irons at every shadow that dares to breathe.", "Gaoler's Tally-Book, last readable page"}, {"The chains were forged by gods, yet broken from the inside like dry twigs.", "Cell Block Inscription"}, {"Look at the gouges in the black rock, and know what crawled out of this pit.", "Warden's Final Log"}}},
    {"sanctum", {{"We knelt upon the polished obsidian and worshiped the warmth that fed our kingdom, blind to the scarred, mutilated god chained in agony right beneath our altar. One reckless strike of the sacred pickaxe cracked the floor. One breath of the waking King turned our golden robes to soot and boiled the blood in our veins.", "Final Prayer of the High Prelate, written in ash on the temple steps"}, {"The great altar stands cold, cracked, and hollow, surrounded by puddles of melted gold offerings that once gleamed in the light of the living crystal. Directly behind it, the temple floor gives way to a gaping, jagged wound torn recklessly into the earth, the fatal shaft through which our ruin climbed into the light.", "Temple Pilgrim's Warning, chiseled into a broken pillar"}, {"Kneel if your knees still bend, traveler, though no merciful god has answered a prayer in these halls since the heart was ripped from the stone. The air here is thick with burning incense and bone-dust, and the zealots who survived the slaughter still claw at their own faces in madness.", "Scroll found inside a cracked bronze censer"}, {"One strike of the pickaxe broke the seal. One breath of the King burned our temple to soot.", "Priest's Last Scratch"}, {"The altar stands cold and empty, yet the wound behind it still bleeds ash.", "Pilgrim's Warning"}}},
    {"deep", {{"Here lies the burned-out cradle of the world, where rivers of boiling metal hiss against islands of jagged black glass, and a fallen god wears our stolen sun inside his broken ribs. At the rotting bottom of the filth, the heartbeat is so loud it rattles the teeth in your skull and shakes loose flakes of stone from the abyss.", "The Prophecy of Cinder and Ash, Final Verse"}, {"No torch or lantern survives this blistering heat, only the blinding, violent glare of the Pyreheart pulsing behind charred bone, casting long, trembling shadows across the walls of fused skulls and slag. Every breath scorches the lungs like swallowed coals.", "Etched onto the inside of a melted dwarven helm"}, {"Beyond the lowest fracture of the earth, where neither pickaxe nor prayer has ever reached, the raw bedrock sweats molten iron and black sulfur. Here the Cinderfire was born in the dark before the sun was lit, pumping its clean, heavy warmth upward through the veins of the stone to keep the young world from freezing.", "Tablet of the First Age, half-submerged in cooled slag"}, {"Here, at the lightless root of the world, we bind the traitor of flame beneath the living weight of the Pyreheart. Let the molten crystal press upon his broken ribs until the stars grow cold, for should his charred hand ever close around the core, the earth itself will bleed to death in ash.", "Oath of the Elder Powers, seared into the raw obsidian before history began"}, {"At the bottom of the filth, the heartbeat is deafening.", "Delver's Final Scrawl"}}},
};
}  // namespace lore
